Fix ``_unescape_char`` corrupting a serialized escaped backslash followed by "n"/"N": the backslash pair is now consumed in a single left-to-right pass, so unescaping a serialized ``C:\\numbers`` yields ``C:\numbers`` again and round-trips with ``_escape_char``. I used GLM-5.3 (Z.ai, via OpenRouter) as my coding agent to analyze the issue, write this fix and its regression tests, and draft this change log entry and the pull request text; I reviewed and validated the change locally. @rahul05ranjan
